# --- recipe
r['recipe'].append({'order':len(r['recipe'])+1,'stage':'modelling','description':'Q4c: differential N-vs-S analysis: Harada+2018 Table 13 (1.7") parsed and compared with our 3-2 at 1.7"; RADEX grids with J=1-0..4-3 (HCN, HCO+), CS 7-6, H13CN 4-3; joint fits of classes A,B,C,D,F (separate n),F2 at N and S with BIC / marginal likelihood, independent 1-0 prediction, N-vs-S option fits (one parameter changes), single-cloud (dv=50) physical quantities, CS discriminator, H13CN prediction, SO scope, literature verification.','software':'python3, numpy, scipy, pandas, RADEX (LAMDA hcn, hco+, cs, h13cn@xpol)','parameters':[A('dv','150 (N/dv scaling to 50 km/s verified)'),A('priors','physT30 (Tkin>=30 K, N<=n+12.5), grid sensitivity'),A('calibration','14% cross-band; 3-2/1-0 flux-scale nuisance 10%')],'scripts':['/workspace/scripts/q4c_lit.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_lit_ratios.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_grid.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_joint.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_ns.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_phys.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_cs.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_h13cn.py','/workspace/scripts/q4c_so_scope.py','/workspace/scripts/build_report_q4c.py']})
# --- interpretation: single Q4 paragraph, CS wording
t=r['interpretation']; i=t.find('Q4 (revised):')
if i>0: t=t[:i]
t=t.replace('and CS 7-6 tracks HCO+ (N=S) not HCN','and CS 7-6/HCO+ 3-2 is the same at N and S within errors (S/N 1.09+-0.48; HCN/CS 1.9x lower at S, 1.2 sigma: weak)')
t+=("Q4 (final): the J=1-0 literature data (Harada+2018 Table 13, 1.7 arcsec: HCN/HCO+ N 0.96, S 0.645) show that ~60% (in log) of the N/S contrast of the 3-2 ratio (1.9-2.0) is already present at 1-0 (1.49): the contrast is mostly J-independent, not excitation. Joint RADEX fits (including 1-0, a separate-density class, BIC/marginal likelihood) prefer both lines thick with HCN more subthermal than HCO+ (Tex ~7 vs ~11 K; HCN tau32 >~2, >~10 for common n; A and separate-n F2 indistinguishable) and reject thin-HCN/abundance-only classes (Delta chi2>=64 (physT30)), also without the Band-5 2-1 ratios; different filling at equal Tex (B) fails the independent 1-0 prediction. Between N and S the data require the HCN (or HCO+) column ratio to change by 1.8-3x, not n or Tkin; N is poorly fitted by every one-zone model, and 8 data cannot constrain two-component models. CS and low-J ratios weakly favour an HCN deficit over an HCO+ enhancement (HCN/CS and HNC/HCO+ lower at S, HCO+/CS equal) but this is <=1.2 sigma in the data. H13CN (HCN/H13CN >8.3 N, >4 S) cannot test opacity: the models predict 17-68. HCN v2=1f limits (alpha<0.03-0.09, Tvib<290-430 K) do not exclude CON-like pumping (200-300 K). SO limits refer to the central 9x6\" beam and to equally extended emission; CH3OH is extended and off-nuclear (<0.013/<0.017 at the nuclei, 0.052 at the Bridge). With X(HCN)=1e-8 the fitted HCN column implies Sigma 2e4-1e5 Msun/pc2, 4-20x above the CO maximum: a tension, not an explanation. The 100-pc-scale source is resolved at 0.25\" (dilution 0.8-0.9).")
r['interpretation']=t
# --- caveats
